<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:22:30 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Trump focused on 'what's important to him': 'Tone-deaf for a normally shrewd populist operator'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Doug Heye, Republican strategist, founder of Douglas Media, and former Communications Director for the Republican National Committee (RNC). As Americans head to the polls, Republicans face a challenge that goes beyond the familiar electoral backlash against an incumbent president. For Heye, Donald Trump's greatest political vulnerability may lie in the widening gap between his rhetoric of economic success and voters' everyday financial anxieties. "For a lot of voters, they see him focused on what's important to him, not what's important to them," Heye explains. Yet he also cautions against interpreting Democratic gains as a sign of renewed confidence in the opposition. Rather than a resurgence of partisan enthusiasm, the elections may expose an electorate increasingly disillusioned with both parties.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a936c1f8-d79a-11f1-927d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-151032-152110-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a936c1f8-d79a-11f1-927d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-151032-152110-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ae6db88e-d79a-11f1-9a41-c3d6717c833f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:05:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump cuts Israeli military aid: $3.8 billion in security assistance slashed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, November 3, said he made a deal with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu for Washington to stop providing $3.8 billion in funding to Israel after the end of this year. FRANCE 24's Jerusalem correspondent, Noga Tarnopolsky, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/243c1fe4-d79e-11f1-9460-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bb8a3c60.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/243c1fe4-d79e-11f1-9460-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bb8a3c60.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b123dec-d79c-11f1-8019-a16362bc26dd</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:01:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Michigan Senate candidate El-Sayed becomes Democrats' rising star</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star</link><description>
In the US midterm elections, Democrat Abdul El-Sayed and Republican Mike Rogers are testing two sharply different strategies to win over voters in one of the nation's premier swing states on Tuesday, November 3, in a closely watched race that could determine control of the Senate. Progressive candidate El-Sayed has so far outpolled his Republican rival and is emerging as one of the Democratic Party's rising stars.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8f73e3a-d798-11f1-8d1b-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T021915Z-175384172-RC21GOAL3HUT-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8f73e3a-d798-11f1-8d1b-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T021915Z-175384172-RC21GOAL3HUT-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6139c40-d795-11f1-a05a-b99ef6dd7b26</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:41:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Michigan candidate El-Sayed pledges to tackle the affordability crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis</link><description>
The cost of living is one of the main concerns for many US voters as the midterm elections get underway. In Michigan, Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed has pledged to "take the money out of politics and put it in your pocket", as FRANCE 24 correspondent Jessica Le Masurier reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86b7508a-d799-11f1-ac61-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-24e76c03.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86b7508a-d799-11f1-ac61-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-24e76c03.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddeb91b0-d797-11f1-95e6-cf155bf49add</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:34:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Paris des arts</category><title>A cultural stroll through Paris with actors François-Xavier Demaison and François Morel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/paris-des-arts/20261103-a-cultural-stroll-through-paris-with-actors-fran%C3%A7ois-xavier-demaison-and-fran%C3%A7ois-morel</link><description>
This week, we bring you a special programme dedicated to theatre. Valérie Fayolle takes us to the Renaissance Theatre, where François-Xavier Demaison takes us behind the scenes of "Laponie". The fiesty comedy shows how a family's holiday gathering can quickly turn into a settling of scores. "Theatre is one of our last collective experiences. It's magnificent, we're in a bubble," he tells us.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/55c7b356-ceb7-11f1-8580-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/1920x1080-main-PARIS-DES-ARTS-demaison.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/55c7b356-ceb7-11f1-8580-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/1920x1080-main-PARIS-DES-ARTS-demaison.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7db8cb22-ceb5-11f1-8aeb-e747d6d4d18c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:30:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie FAYOLLE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>King Charles says he has greater understanding of 'horrors' of slavery, falls short of apology</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology</link><description>
King Charles III told the heads of 56 Commonwealth countries on Tuesday that he has a greater understanding of the horrors of slavery, calling it a "shameful chapter of history". This comes as Prime Minister Andy Burnham said he was open to the United Kingdom apologising for the transatlantic slave trade. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a616320-d799-11f1-b243-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26307507185418.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a616320-d799-11f1-b243-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26307507185418.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d5f02c8-d797-11f1-b6e5-4f05fbfd3658</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:26:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a616320-d799-11f1-b243-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26307507185418.jpg">© Matias Delacroix, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Your donut, your vote': Texas group uses free food to attract young voters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters</link><description>
US voters on Tuesday headed to the polls in midterm elections that could shape the political future of the country. But navigating the voting process can sometimes discourage voters – particularly younger ones. In Texas, an organisation reached out to them directly by handing out free food, to then help them overcome these obstacles. FRANCE 24's Special envoy Tarek Kai reports from Austin. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff05cc8c-d790-11f1-a95a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8705fe98.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff05cc8c-d790-11f1-a95a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8705fe98.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75d1b972-d78f-11f1-8419-a7b99722fd37</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:26:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Political parallels in France and the US: Anger at the ballot box and in the streets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets</link><description>
Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre. We take a look at some of the common issues causing this anger on both sides of the Atlantic, including the rising cost of living, a loss of faith in institutions and an eroding of the social contract. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1bfa7e-d78f-11f1-a058-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-667ff99f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1bfa7e-d78f-11f1-a058-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-667ff99f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e966c42-d78d-11f1-800f-797807b5100c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:21:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: All eyes on crucial Michigan Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race</link><description>
In the US midterm elections, the Senate race in Michigan has been one of the most closely watched in the country. It took an unexpected turn on Sunday after Democratic Congresswoman Haley Stevens endorsed Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic nominee Abdul El-Sayed. Both candidates made their final pitches to voters during campaign rallies on Monday evening, November 2. FRANCE 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f194c78c-d791-11f1-8a10-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ec985e87.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f194c78c-d791-11f1-8a10-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ec985e87.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc66656c-d790-11f1-8181-77a18b1366df</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 15:15:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says US will halt $4 billion in aid to Israel after end of the year</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-trump-says-us-will-halt-4-billion-in-aid-to-israel-after-end-of-this-year</link><description>
President Donald Trump on Tuesday said that the United States will stop $4 billion in funding to Israel after the end of this year. While speaking to Fox News' Fox and Friends, the US president added that Israel no longer needed the aid from Washington, and that some politicians were using the funding to criticise Republicans. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f65d6a6-070d-11f1-95d4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/t-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f65d6a6-070d-11f1-95d4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/t-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49ec03e8-d790-11f1-9022-651442198644</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:35:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f65d6a6-070d-11f1-95d4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/t-1.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>2026 Prix Goncourt: France's prestigious literary prize awarded to Philippe Jaenada</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-2026-prix-goncourt-france-s-prestigious-literary-prize-awarded-to-philippe-jaenada</link><description>
France’s prestigious literary prize “The Goncourt” was awarded on Monday to writer Philippe Jaenada. The prize carries a symbolic reward of only 10 euros, but results in considerable recognition and book sales for the winning author. FRANCE 24’s Culture reporter Olivia Salazar-Winspear reports from the Parisian restaurant where the jury made the call.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0b23f4e-d78e-11f1-b886-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-131820-132143-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0b23f4e-d78e-11f1-b886-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-131820-132143-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c618194a-d78e-11f1-9d70-e574bb1b4eb7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:21:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Americans vote in key midterms set to upend Trump presidency</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-americans-vote-in-key-midterms-set-to-upend-trump-presidency</link><description>
Americans voted on Tuesday in pivotal midterm elections with Democrats hoping to seize control of Congress and impose the first significant checks on Donald Trump's chaotic second term in the White House. Republicans losing the House would give Democrats the power to stall Trump's legislative agenda and launch sweeping investigations of his administration. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington, DC.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0961fbc0-d790-11f1-8ddc-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-140150-140543-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0961fbc0-d790-11f1-8ddc-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-140150-140543-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e8dca34-d790-11f1-8065-c57a8f2369b6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:18:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli opposition leaders vow to remove Netanyahu quickly but path unclear</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-israeli-opposition-leaders-vow-to-remove-netanyahu-quickly-but-path-unclear</link><description>
The Israeli opposition bloc led by Gadi Eisenkot pledged Tuesday to form a government quickly to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu but remained unclear on how, with divisions over whether to ally with Arab lawmakers. Arab-majority parties last week won 19 seats in the 120-member parliament. Eisenkot's diverse opposition bloc won 48 seats while Netanyahu's camp secured 53, of which 27 are from his Likud party.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0f43940-d790-11f1-a2b5-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-141718-141934-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0f43940-d790-11f1-a2b5-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-141718-141934-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e5ef12bc-d790-11f1-bdf0-0d5aad648991</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:17:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterm elections: A referendum on President Donald Trump?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-a-referendum-on-president-donald-trump</link><description>
Americans deliver their verdict on Donald Trump's tumultuous first term in midterm elections that threaten to shatter his grip on Washington, with Democrats poised to seize the House and within striking distance of the Senate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87057ba4-d779-11f1-a078-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-07859cae.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87057ba4-d779-11f1-a078-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-07859cae.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">054de1e2-d778-11f1-8c91-1731a2a44c48</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:56:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Californians vote on ballot initiative to impose one-time tax on billionaires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261103-californians-vote-on-ballot-initiative-to-impose-one-time-tax-on-billionaires</link><description>
This Tuesday, Californians are voting on a landmark plan to impose a one-time tax on billionaires to fund the state's healthcare system. We take a closer look. Also on the show: global oil prices fell sharply on the eve of the US midterm elections. This came after Iran said it was holding intensive talks through mediators towards negotiating peace and signalled that it was ready to reopen the Strait of Hormuz if the US accepted its conditions. Both Brent and WTI fell by around 8 percent. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e86a7986-d78c-11f1-89d7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bd8a0acf.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e86a7986-d78c-11f1-89d7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bd8a0acf.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26f6556a-d708-11f1-8842-316b50402d90</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:51:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland foils attempted 'provocation' on Russian border, PM Tusk says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says</link><description>
Prime Minister Donald Tusk said Tuesday that Poland prevented an attempted "provocation" on its border with the Russian exclave of Kaliningrad overnight. He gave few details but said Polish security forces prevented any incident from happening.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1af66d0-d789-11f1-91be-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23108425555797.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1af66d0-d789-11f1-91be-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23108425555797.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ab2666c-d788-11f1-bfba-b907054521ed</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:39:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1af66d0-d789-11f1-91be-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23108425555797.jpg">© Michal Kosc, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Supreme court rejects Trump request to set aside 20,000 California ballots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-request-to-set-aside-20-000-california-ballots</link><description>
The US Supreme Court rejected the Trump administration’s push to force California to set aside 20,000 ballots from people the federal government claims are noncitizens, a decision that came hours before the final day of voting in the pivotal midterm elections. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/451554a6-d78a-11f1-8a9f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7d06555a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/451554a6-d78a-11f1-8a9f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7d06555a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6189e2ac-d779-11f1-aa27-813072c02d5d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:27:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What could happen if Donald Trump loses US midterm elections?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-what-could-happen-if-donald-trump-loses-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Americans head to the polls on Tuesday in pivotal midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to seize control of Congress and impose the first significant checks on Donald Trump's second term in the White House. But what could happen in the United States if Republicans lose control of Congress? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29f7ba36-d77d-11f1-af13-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5031862c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29f7ba36-d77d-11f1-af13-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5031862c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fce5bba6-d77c-11f1-bc81-23d19c741ad6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:24:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'I love giving debut novelists a chance': Shakespeare and Company's Adam Biles</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261103-i-love-giving-debut-novelists-a-chance-shakespeare-and-company-s-adam-biles</link><description>
The literary director of the English-language Paris bookshop Shakespeare and Company says that the shop has achieved such notoriety that invitations to authors to appear there are usually accepted. Adam Biles says the shop enjoys inviting both famous authors to speak there, as well as debut authors who deserve the exposure. Adam hosts the events himself, and over the years has interviewed hundreds of different literary figures of varying notoriety. Many of the shop's guests speak to us in Perspective before or after their appearances. We spoke to Adam in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03e362-d787-11f1-baf5-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-200f2a76.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03e362-d787-11f1-baf5-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-200f2a76.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">602a6256-d76a-11f1-b28d-dd8d7db66563</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 13:24:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Could a blue wave widen the centrist-progressive divide among Democrats ahead of 2028?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-could-a-blue-wave-widen-the-centrist-progressive-divide-among-democrats-ahead-of-2028</link><description>
As the US approaches the midterms, the contest is emerging as a referendum on Donald Trump, the resilience of American democratic institutions and the ability of a divided Democratic Party to transform widespread public dissatisfaction into a coherent political alternative. With some Republicans now seeking to distance themselves from Trump, Katy Hull, Assistant Professor of American Studies at the University of Amsterdam, suggests that the president's highly populist and personalised approach to politics is becoming an electoral liability. Philip Turle observes Republican voters turning towards the opposition "as a form of protest against Donald Trump", rather than an endorsement of the Democrats.
